                            <comment id="15740286" author="moon" created="Sun, 11 Dec 2016 20:25:45 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I think we need to remove them from common.sh.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;As you mentioned, zeppelin used to overriding zeppelin-site.xml by environment variable. And advertised this behavior.&lt;br/&gt;
&lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/docs/install/install.md#apache-zeppelin-configuration&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/zeppelin/blob/master/docs/install/install.md#apache-zeppelin-configuration&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Changing this will be big user experience change.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;One reason in the beginning make environment variable override zeppelin-site.xml was, it&apos;s easy to add environment variable into conf/zeppelin-env.sh programmatically, via shell script, etc.&lt;br/&gt;
In comparison modifying conf/zeppelin-site.xml programmatically requires little more skills.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I think it helps some deployment such as containerized deployment or run virtual machine image on AWS, to let user easily override configurations programmatically on start up.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
